.TH A2SITEMGR 1 "2026-07-06" "a2tools 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
a2sitemgr \- opinionated Apache virtual\-host manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B a2sitemgr
.RB [ \-d " " \fIDOMAIN\fR]
.RB [ \-\-fqdn " " \fIDOMAIN\fR]
.RB [ \-m | \-\-mode
.RB { domain | proxypass | swc }]
.RB [ \-p " " \fIPORT\fR]
.RB [ \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR]
.RB [ \-s | \-\-secured ]
.RB [ \-r " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.RB [ \-\-registrar " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR]
.RB [ \-ni | \-\-non\-interactive ]
.RB [ \-\-setInitDNSRecords ]
.RB [ \-o | \-\-override ]
.RB [ \-\-sync ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBa2sitemgr\fR creates Apache2 virtual hosts using a small set of
opinionated, repeatable templates and obtains TLS certificates via
\fBcertbot\fR.
.PP
All arguments are named flags. Positional arguments are not accepted;
the FQDN must be supplied via \fB\-d\fR / \fB\-\-fqdn\fR.
.PP
Three modes are supported:
.TP
.B domain
Standard vhost for a single base domain. Requests a wildcard certificate
for the base domain using the ACME DNS\-01 challenge via the configured
\fBfqdnmgr\fR hooks.
.TP
.B proxypass
Reverse\-proxied subdomain backed by the base domain's existing wildcard
certificate. Use \fB\-\-secured\fR when the upstream service speaks HTTPS.
.TP
.B swc
Subdomain wildcard. A single \fImail.*\fR vhost serves the same subdomain
across every base domain managed by \fBa2tools\fR, reusing the base
domains' existing certificates.
.PP
If a domain is owned by a registrar that \fBfqdnmgr\fR knows about,
\fBa2sitemgr\fR will verify ownership, set the required DNS records and
wait for propagation before invoking \fBcertbot\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-fqdn " " \fIDOMAIN\fR
Domain or subdomain to manage. Required.
.RB "For " "swc" " mode pass a wildcard such as " "mail.*" "."
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " { \fBdomain\fR | \fBproxypass\fR | \fBswc\fR }
Vhost mode. Default: \fBdomain\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Local port to reverse proxy to (proxypass mode only).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-secured
Upstream service is HTTPS (proxypass mode only).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registrar " " \fIREGISTRAR\fR
Registrar slug (e.g. \fBnamecheap.com\fR) used to verify ownership and
configure DNS records.
.TP
.BR \-ni ", " \-\-non\-interactive
Do not prompt. Fail if required information is missing.
.TP
.BR \-\-setInitDNSRecords
Set the initial DNS records required for HTTPS before certificate
issuance.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-override
When used with \fB\-\-setInitDNSRecords\fR, delete all existing DNS
records before setting the initial ones. Without this flag, existing
records are preserved and initial records are added/updated.
.TP
.BR \-\-sync
When used with \fB\-\-setInitDNSRecords\fR, block until DNS propagation
is confirmed.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print progress on the controlling terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the embedded usage text and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred (certbot failure, DNS propagation failure, missing
dependency, etc.). Details are logged to
\fB/var/log/a2tools/fqdnmgr.log\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/a2tools/domain.conf
Per\-domain vhost parameters.
.TP
.I /etc/apache2/sites\-available/
Generated vhost configs.
.TP
.I /var/lib/a2tools/domains.db
SQLite database tracking the domains managed by \fBa2tools\fR.
.TP
.I /var/log/a2tools/
Operational logs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a vhost for a single base domain:
.RS
.nf
sudo a2sitemgr -d example.com
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a ProxyPass subdomain that points at a local container:
.RS
.nf
sudo a2sitemgr -d app.example.com --mode proxypass -p 1234
sudo a2sitemgr -d app.example.com --mode proxypass -p 8443 --secured
.fi
.RE
.PP
Serve a single subdomain across every managed base domain:
.RS
.nf
sudo a2sitemgr -d 'mail.*' --mode swc
.fi
.RE
.PP
Set initial DNS records and wait for propagation before issuing the
wildcard certificate:
.RS
.nf
sudo a2sitemgr -d example.com --setInitDNSRecords --sync -r namecheap.com -v
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR a2certrenew (1),
.BR a2wcrecalc (1),
.BR a2wcrecalc\-dms (1),
.BR fqdnmgr (1),
.BR fqdncredmgr (1),
.BR certbot (1),
.BR apache2ctl (8)
.PP
